1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,520
IELTS Mock Test 1.

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:05,680
You will hear a number of different recordings and you will have to answer

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,080
questions on what you hear.

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,920
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,480
have a chance to check your work.

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,200
All the recordings will be played once only.

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,160
The test is in four parts.

8
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,680
Now turn to part one.

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:24,920
Part one.

10
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:33,760
You will shortly hear a conversation between a prospective tenant calling to

11
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,640
know about some vacant accommodation.

12
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:40,000
First you have some time to look at questions one to five.

13
00:00:54,920 --> 00:01:14,920
Now we shall begin.

14
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:19,080
You should answer the questions as you listen because you will not hear the

15
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,480
recording a second time.

16
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:24,640
Listen carefully and answer questions one to five.

17
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:29,280
Hello?

18
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,240
Yes, hello.

19
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,960
My name is Roger Peters and I'm looking for an apartment.

20
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,880
I saw your ad in the paper about a vacant flat.

21
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,800
I would like to inquire about it.

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,360
Ah, okay.

23
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:47,520
Yes, I got that ad published.

24
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:52,080
I do have a vacant flat and it is still available.

25
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,320
Ah, then I do have the right number.

26
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:58,200
Could you please tell me more about the flat?

27
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:02,120
From the ad in the paper, it sounds nice.

28
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,280
I'm in dire need of a place to shift to.

29
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,800
Why are you looking for a place to shift?

30
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:14,760
There are several reasons why I'm looking to move, but most of all, I want to lower

31
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:19,480
my costs and also move to a place closer to my workplace.

32
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:23,600
The flat you are offering meets the criteria.

33
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,000
I see.

34
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,120
Where are you living now and how much are you paying for rent?

35
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:34,240
I'm currently living on the East End off Highland Boulevard.

36
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:41,200
I live in a two bedroom flat and I'm paying $800 a month plus utilities.

37
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,560
It's in that new tower, you know, Brannan Complex.

38
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:49,400
Oh, yes, that is an exclusive area.

39
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,640
Indeed, it is.

40
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:55,800
Can I have a little more information about the flat you offer?

41
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,960
What would you like to know?

42
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,080
Well, how spacious is it?

43
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:06,840
Well, it's big enough to accommodate a family of four to five members.

44
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:14,680
It has a living room, two bedrooms, dining room, kitchen, washroom and a spacious balcony.

45
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:21,000
Well, there are three of us in my family and that sounds like it would suit us nicely.

46
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,080
Is it fully furnished?

47
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,240
What about utilities?

48
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:33,320
Yes, it's fully furnished and utilities included are water, gas and electricity.

49
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:37,400
You will have to arrange for your own landline for telephone.

50
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,160
Nice.

51
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:43,400
And what is the precise location of the building it is housed in?

52
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,360
It's on Flayler's Tower.

53
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:49,800
It's a fairly new building built two to three years back.

54
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:03,720
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions six to ten.

55
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:40,120
Now listen carefully and answer questions six to ten.

56
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:45,240
Oh, that sounds great.

57
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,240
How much is the rent?

58
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:51,800
The rent is five hundred and fifty dollars per month.

59
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:56,200
Oh, that is going to burn a hole in my pocket.

60
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:01,880
Well, as I said, it is fully furnished and includes all the utilities.

61
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,920
Yes, you did say that.

62
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:12,520
Now, if you do pay in advance, say six months in advance, which will be three thousand three

63
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:17,480
hundred dollars, you'll get a discount of five percent off the total rent.

64
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:22,520
So this means you want to sign an agreement for six months?

65
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:28,760
I would prefer this, but you do have the option to pay rent every month.

66
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,400
So the choice is yours.

67
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:37,000
Well, it would be difficult for me to forecast six months rent in advance.

68
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,560
I'd much rather go from month to month rent.

69
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,040
What about parking?

70
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,640
Parking is available next to the entrance.

71
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,680
And is this a secured parking?

72
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:51,880
I mean, is there security present?

73
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:53,880
Yes, of course.

74
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:58,680
There is a security guard twenty four hours a day at the entrance.

75
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,240
Is there anything else you would like to know?

76
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,000
Yes.

77
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,560
How far is it from the shopping mall?

78
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,560
And is there a park nearby for the children to play?

79
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:16,120
Well, there is a park and playground on the complex, which the children can play in.

80
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:19,800
Unfortunately, there is no large mall nearby.

81
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:25,560
The nearest school is three kilometer away, but they do have a pickup.

82
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:30,360
There is a fair number of stores nearby for day to day shopping.

83
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,040
And when does this flat get ready to shift?

84
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:38,280
Well, after you fill out the application

85
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:43,800
and pass the credit and background check, you could move in about a week.

86
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,360
Ah, OK.

87
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,280
Is there anything else?

88
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:56,440
Yes, you do need to pay the first month's rent and a security amount of five hundred dollars.

89
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,400
Why is there a security deposit?

90
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:05,640
Mainly to ensure that you do not leave the apartment in a dilapidated condition.

91
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,880
Is it refundable?

92
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:13,160
Only if you leave the apartment clean and in good shape.

93
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,040
When can I come by to view the flat and make the arrangements?

94
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,200
We can meet tomorrow.

95
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,600
Very well, I'll come then.

96
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,600
Thank you.

97
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:34,040
That is the end of part one.

98
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:38,600
You now have half a minute to check your answers.

99
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:14,600
Now turn to part two.
